{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich and was directed by david fincher.\n\nthe film starts with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a sophomore at harvard university. mark is a brilliant computer science student who is also a bit of a social outcast. he is obsessed with the idea of creating a website that will allow harvard students to connect with each other. with the help of his roommates and fellow students eduardo saverin (andrew garfield) and dustin moskovitz (joseph mazzello), mark creates a website called \"thefacebook\".\n\nthe website quickly becomes a huge success, and mark becomes a celebrity on campus. however, things start to get complicated when mark and eduardo have different ideas about how to run the website, and mark starts to work with sean parker (justin timberlake), the co-founder of napster. sean is a smooth-talking entrepreneur who sees the potential of facebook and wants to help mark take it to the next level.\n\nmeanwhile, the winklevoss twins, cameron and tyler (played by armie hammer), who are also harvard students, claim that mark stole their idea for thefacebook. they hire a lawyer and sue mark and facebook for intellectual property theft.\n\nthe film is a fascinating look at the early days of facebook and the people who created it. the cast is excellent, with jesse eisenberg giving a standout performance as mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is also great as eduardo saverin, who is portrayed as a loyal friend who gets pushed aside by mark's growing ambition.\n\nthe film's script, written by aaron sorkin, is witty and engaging, and the direction by david fincher is sleek and stylish. the movie's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy.\n\none of the things that makes the social network so compelling is its exploration of the complexities of friendship and loyalty. mark and eduardo's relationship is particularly interesting, as they go from being close friends to bitter enemies. the film also raises questions about the ethics of entrepreneurship and the consequences of success.\n\noverall, the social network is a great film that is both entertaining and thought-provoking. it's a must-see for anyone who is interested in the story of facebook and the people who created it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24996495246887207}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05464606732130051}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.18567566573619843}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -9.298368240706623e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.218656047465629e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.017032857984304428}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015200339839793742}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00016094549209810793}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08091060072183609}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.11775506287813187}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017488384619355202}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0036843856796622276}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00590532785281539}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.06923678517341614}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0008205560734495521}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04554614797234535}, {"token": " based", "logprob": -2.0986528396606445}, {"token": " on", "log